  "scope": [
    "Version 10 binds the original action observer inside chunk startup before actions become accepted. Frozen controls expose the exact version-7 recording identity; every subsequent owned chunk explicitly captures its next observer.",
    "Observer admission reads only an own data callback and snapshots it before asynchronous startup. Bound decline never falls back to a global observer. Manual chunks and legacy completion behavior retain their existing contracts.",
    "Owned action steps reference every original stack in the original journal. Parent association checks the exact step object in the original TestInfo map and locally removes stale step zones before creating ordinary API steps or associating assertions.",
    "Closing original action admission suppresses subsequent step publication and late completion events while allowing original library call bookkeeping and public outcomes to complete.",
    "Source-only journal references create no synthetic events or early file reads. They share the ordinary source policy, deduplication, 4096-path/1-MiB metadata/32768-character limits and final retained UTF-8 ingestion. Disabled source capture does not inspect input stacks."
  ],
  "verification": [
    "Each runtime passes 15 action-step, 17 archive, 24 journal, 13 assembly and eight finalizer unit groups, plus packed private integration.",
    "The actual owned-runner fixture passes six attempts and eight library chunks per run on Bun and Node 22/24 with headless shell, and Bun with full Chrome. Source on/off, reuse across chunks and successor actions inside old test.step and expect zones are exercised.",
    "Library action step IDs and titles align with their original runner journal. Retained parents belong to that same journal. The pinned trace loader and model accept every final archive; helper source bytes match the final UTF-8 file and are read once per retained source-enabled attempt. Source-disabled attempts perform no source reads.",
    "Callback mutation, accessors, proxies, decline, manual replacement, stale handles, old completions and callback faults preserve original action and export ownership. Source admission rejects unsafe input without invoking caller code and shares limits with ordinary journal events.",
    "Bun additionally passes manual trace units, native manual tracing, disabled runner tracing and declaration checks. Every frozen source, compiled artifact, browser and driver identity remains unchanged. Retained ZIPs pass CRC checks and all observed watchdog processes retire cleanly.",
    "Affected provenance was regenerated and checked in the frozen verification view, then regenerated and checked against the committed native peer parent plus the exact verified runner changes."
  ],
  "reproduce": [
    "Build all four packages and run tools/typecheck.mjs with pinned Bun.",
    "Run tools/test-runner-trace-steps.mjs, tools/test-runner-trace-archives.mjs, tools/test-runner-trace-journal.mjs, tools/test-trace-archive-assembly.mjs, tools/test-runner-trace-finalizer.mjs and tools/test-packed-runner-integration.mjs on Bun and Node 22/24.",
    "Run tools/run-runner-trace-source-tests.mjs on those runtimes with explicit verified browser and driver paths; repeat with full Chrome on Bun.",
    "Run tools/test-manual-tracing.mjs, tools/run-manual-trace-tests.mjs and tools/run-runner-trace-off-tests.mjs on Bun. Use external watchdogs."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This focused verification reuses the accepted pre-API native driver for ordinary browser actions. It does not verify the combined native API/runner build or rerun Rust, full-core, Linux, package-manager layouts or performance gates.",
    "The actual fixture privately assembles retained library archives with the original runner journal. The production finalizer still owns only the journal; automatic enrollment, shared screenshot coordination, per-attempt capture admission and attached API capture remain unfinished.",
    "Public automatic trace policies remain unsupported. No release, publication or fastest-framework claim is made."
  ]
